nymous Sensory Transduction. Rockefeller University Press, New York, NY. 133&#x02013;150.</citation></ref><ref id="Kauppetal1989"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaupp</surname><given-names>U.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Niidome</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanabe</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Terada</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>B&#x000f6;nigk</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>St&#x000fc;hmer</surname><given-names>W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>N.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kangawa</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsuo</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirose</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary structure and functional expression from complementary DNA of the rod photoreceptor cyclic GMP-gated channel</article-title><source>Nature.</source><volume>342</volume><year>1989</year><fpage>762</fpage><lpage>766</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2481236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="N0x27d55d0N0x3296630"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>K&#x000f6;rschen</surname><given-names>H.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Illing</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Seifert</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sesti</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gotzes</surname><given-names>S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Colville</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000fc;ller</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dos&#x000e9;</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Godde</surname><given-names>M.</